commit 288324ee6e95968cd76985380991f062db11b5a7
feat(init): smart plugin defaults from cwd, scalable picker, --yes

Make `dprint init` work well when info.json has many plugins and pick
sensible defaults automatically.

- Pre-select plugins by scanning the current directory for files that
  match each plugin's file extensions / file names (bounded scan), in
  info.json order. Drops the now-unused `selected` info.json property.
- Multi-select picker now scrolls to fit the terminal height and
  supports type-to-filter, so long plugin lists stay usable.
- Show each plugin's file extensions beside its name.
- Add `dprint init --yes` to skip the prompt and accept the defaults;
  also auto-skipped when there's no interactive terminal (ex. CI).

